# What Railway does not need in the upload.
#
# `railway up` uploads a snapshot of the working tree before anything is
# built. The tracked tree is 43 MB and 33 MB of that is `docs/` — mostly
# `docs/uat-screenshots`, several hundred PNGs of the officer portal and the
# agent PWA. A CLI upload of that timed out, and a retry on the half-finished
# state answered "Failed to create code snapshot", which reads like a repo
# problem and is not one.
#
# Nothing excluded here is copied by any image. Every Dockerfile in this
# repository copies exactly `package.json`, `package-lock.json`,
# `packages/shared` and its own `apps/<name>` — none of them reads `docs/`,
# `.github/`, a backup or the local storage directory. Checked by listing the
# COPY sources of all four before writing this file.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE ADDED HERE. `apps/api/assets/fonts/*.ttf` and
# `apps/api/src/db/migrations/*.sql` look like data rather than code and are
# neither: the API build runs `scripts/copy-assets.mjs`, which puts both into
# `dist` and aborts the build if they are missing. An image that cannot spell
# ₦ or cannot migrate is the failure this note exists to prevent.
#
# This file is gitignore-shaped and only affects the CLI upload. A deploy
# triggered from GitHub clones the repository instead and ignores it.

# Screenshots and the certification paperwork — 33 MB, read by people, never
# by a build.
docs/

# CI definitions run on GitHub, not in the image.
.github/

# Never in a snapshot: installed, built, or local to one machine.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
.git/

# Local runtime state. `storage/` is the object-storage driver's own directory
# and the image creates it at startup; a copy from a laptop is not wanted.
backups/
storage/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
